DATABASE SCHEMA (live)
  table interviewees (existing, extended)
    id, name, bio, contact (PRIVATE), status, role_tag, instagram_followers, facebook_followers,
    last_contacted, returning_guest, note, archived, sort_order, created_at
    + photo_url     text          full public URL, set on approval
    + social_handle text          stored as @handle
    + invite_token  uuid unique   the private form link secret
    + published     bool default false   controls website visibility
  table interviewee_submissions
    id, interviewee_id -> interviewees.id (cascade), name 1-120, bio <=500, social_handle <=100,
    photo_path, review_status pending|approved|rejected, reviewer_note, submitted_at, reviewed_at
  storage bucket interviewee-photos
    public read yes, 2 MB max, jpeg/png/webp, upload path <invite_token>/<timestamp>-<rand>.jpg
  functions
    get_interviewee_form(p_token)                        [anon, authenticated]  security definer
    submit_interviewee_form(p_token,name,bio,handle,photo_path)  [anon, authenticated]  security definer
    is_valid_invite_folder(p_folder)                     [anon, authenticated]  used by storage policy
    approve_submission(p_submission_id, p_note)          [authenticated ONLY]   security invoker

ACCESS RULES (verified 2026-09-28 by role-switch tests)
  anon:
    - interviewees: SELECT only safe columns, only published=true AND archived=false
    - denied: contact, invite_token, updates, interviewee_submissions (all), approve_submission
    - photo_path in submit must start with caller's own token (else "Invalid photo")
    - storage upload only into a valid token folder
  authenticated: full access (RLS "authenticated full access")

FLOWS (built)
  form:      <site>/submit.html?t=<invite_token>
             load -> get_interviewee_form; bad/missing token -> "This link isn't working"
             photo resized in browser (max 1400px, JPEG, stepped quality to fit 2 MB; input cap 25 MB)
             upload -> submit_interviewee_form -> "Thank you" state; same link re-editable (replaces pending)
             handle accepts @name, name, or instagram.com/name; saved as @name
  website:   fetch published rows (anon REST), order sort_order then name
             keeps existing placeholder cards until at least 1 approved profile exists
             placeholder silhouette if no photo; modal shows "@handle on Instagram" link
  tracker:   tab "Website Approvals" (pink badge = pending count)
               - Waiting for approval: live vs submitted side by side, changes outlined
               - Approve & publish (approve_submission) | Reject (note, internal)
               - Form links table: Copy form link | Show/Hide on website | New link (rotates token)
               - Recently reviewed (last 15)
             Interviewee board cards: "On website" / "Profile to approve" tags + "Form link" button
             every action writes activity_log (entity interviewee, field "website profile"/"on website"/"form link")
  links:     built as https://chasingthesash.com/submit.html?t=<token>  (SITE_URL const in tracker.html)

